From 0b904fc648ac4625c7e8e3e77e5b8e1ac8368986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:22:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(gpui): release image pixels after upload; add a
 painted-text primitive

RenderImage::new_releasable creates a single-frame image whose CPU
pixels are dropped once a window has uploaded them to its sprite atlas,
while only one window is open. A later atlas miss (a window opened
afterwards, or a lost device) rebuilds them through the image's pixel
source; when that fails the sprite is skipped instead of panicking.
paint_image and patch_animated_image share the upload path.

PaintedText is a scene primitive that rebuilds a 7TV-style name paint
per pixel: stroke rings and a gradient or image fill drawn through a
glyph mask, then drop shadows from precomputed weights. Its mask is an
8-bit atlas tile (AtlasKey::PaintMask, PaintMask) stacking the coverage
and one block per shadow; the fill can sample an image frame from the
polychrome atlas, and patch_animated_image swaps that frame without a
redraw. Window::paint_painted_text, App/Window::drop_paint_mask and
PlatformWindow::supports_painted_text expose it. The Direct3D 11
renderer draws it with a new shader (mask at t0, instances at t1, fill
at t2); other renderers report no support and skip it.
